I second {la van}. Lojban's semantics are not fully specified, and even
parsing it correctly is tricky in some cases. Also, expecting your users to
learn lojban is unrealistic.

You might want to look into Attempto Controlled English [1], but I'd focus
on getting the query language right and general and helping users construct
queries rather than parsing human language.

Also, I tried to use the advanced search on your website and got an error.
Steps taken
1. Click on "advanced search"
2. Select "Final Destination", "Mr. Game & Watch", and "Sheik (If you
should only be able to select one of each category, you should be using
radio buttons, not check boxes)
3. Click on "continue"
4. Get uninformative webpage that says "Error" and "Sorry, an error
occurred."

[1]: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attempto_Controlled_English


